  "body": "Found during #3746 (PR #3823), after the merge of #3818 (`7f4915a6d`, the in-plane ring links of #3747).\n\n## What happens\n\nSetup: `crates/app/tests/offset_pass_start.rs`, `fig8_world()`, 2D Offset, Pass starts at Outside, EM-0800-4FL, the Arc entry (`offset_op_entered(..., PassStart::Outside, Entry3D::Arc)`).\n\nThe pass link at the end of a piece at (47.429, -39.000) does not keep down. The tool lifts to clearance and rapids 162 mm across the part to the next pass start at (46.482, 123.140). The same lift occurs at Z 12.000, Z 2.000 and Z 1.500. One more occurs at Z 1.500 to (-46.500, 123.542).\n\nThe link notes say:\n- `link: the tool lifted to the retract plane 6 time(s) instead of the keep-down level/pass link - the in-plane link would cross a cut planned on that plane; ... (first lift at (47.429, -39.000), Z 12.000)`\n- `link: the tool lifted to the retract plane 6 time(s) instead of the keep-down level/pass link - the in-plane link would leave the area that keeps the tool off the part; ... (first lift at (46.488, 123.257), Z 12.000)`\n\nEach next start is in material. The entry code (`entry_restart`) tries, in this order:\n1. the air entry of #3746;\n2. the ramp along the pass;\n3. a clear helix.\n\nNone fits, so the start is entered with the named plunge: `entry: the pass start (46.482, 123.140) at Z 12.000 is in material and the arc's lead room is blocked, and no ramp fits clear of prior cuts - plunged into material at the plunge feed`.\n\n## Why the entry code cannot fix it\n\nThe start stands inside ring 0, the walk along the stock edge, which is cut first. Each in-plane lead from the air crosses ring 0 at the cut Z, and the verifier's Crossing law holds such a post. The start column has no room for a helix clear of the earlier cuts. The piece is too short for the ramp. Only a link that stays down through cut material (for example along ring 0) reaches the start. That is link or order code (`pass_link`, `ring_links`, `level_order`).\n\n## Done means\n\n- `fig8_outside_offset_has_no_plunge_into_material` (`crates/app/tests/offset_pass_start.rs`) is green. Remove its known-fail marker in the same PR.\n- On fig8 Outside, no pass link lifts across the part to a start in material without a named reason that the status line shows.\n",
